# Documentation SDLC (always)

Agents own `docs/` quality. Read [docs/sdlc/agent-phases.md](../../docs/sdlc/agent-phases.md) for **planning** vs **implementation** vs **ship**.

## Before every commit / push / PR

1. Identify **phase** (planning | implementation).
2. Read [docs/DOC-MAP.md](../../docs/DOC-MAP.md) and update every listed doc **in the same branch**.
3. Run **`/sync-documentation`** before opening or updating a PR.
4. Dependency engine implementation: **`/ship-dependency-feature`**.

## Planning phase

- **Read:** [roadmap/active.md](../../docs/roadmap/active.md), [roadmap/backlog/](../../docs/roadmap/backlog/), relevant `docs/specs/`.
- **Write:** active/backlog promotion, spec design, product docs.
- **Do not:** [changelog.md](../../docs/history/changelog.md) or remove active rows until the feature is **shipped**.

## Implementation phase

- **Write:** code/config/tests + DOC-MAP targets in the **same PR**.
- **Ship:** remove task from active, append changelog, update inventory/README per DOC-MAP.
- **WIP:** keep task in active; no changelog.

## Non-negotiables

- Never leave **shipped** work in [roadmap/active.md](../../docs/roadmap/active.md).
- PR body: **Phase** + **Documentation** section (paths or explicit none).
